{#-
  title.tmpl - Page title with breadcrumbs and taxonomy links

  Renders:
  - Breadcrumb navigation (Home >> Section >> Subsection >> Page)
    * One clickable » per ancestor level; clicking it expands the
      full trail (no hover expansion, so the layout never shifts)
    * Last breadcrumb (current page) stays visible
  - Fallback to simple title link if no breadcrumbs
  - Taxonomy links (tags, categories, etc.) if present

  Variables:
  - breadcrumbs: Array of {name, link} tuples for navigation
  - link: URL for the page title (used when no breadcrumbs)
  - title: Page title text
  - taxonomies: Hash of taxonomy terms (tags, categories, etc.)

  Used by: post.tmpl, gallery.tmpl, folder_index feature, and manually in code
-#}
<h1 class="primary">
  {% if breadcrumbs|length > 0 %}
  <nav aria-label="breadcrumb" class="breadcrumb">
    {% for item in breadcrumbs %}
      {% if loop.last %}
      <a href="{{ item.link }}" class="">{{ item.name }}</a>
      {% else %}
      <a href="{{ item.link }}" class="breadcrumb-collapsed">{{ item.name }}</a>
      <span class="breadcrumb-sep breadcrumb-toggle" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Show breadcrumb trail" title="Show path" onclick="this.closest('nav').classList.toggle('expanded')" onkeydown="if(event.key==='Enter'||event.key===' '){event.preventDefault();this.closest('nav').classList.toggle('expanded')}">»</span>
      {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </nav>
  {% else %}
  <a href="{{link}}">{{title}}</a>
  {% endif %}
</h1>

{% if taxonomies | length > 1 %}
<nav>
  <ul>
    {% for k,v in taxonomies %}
    <li>
      {{k | link }} :
      {% for term in v %}
      {{term | link}}
      {% endfor%}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</nav>
{% endif %}
